_(1) For the purposes of preventing money laundering, where a limited partnership registered in Scotland has general partners at least one of those must have an active UK bank account.
(2) Where a limited partnership registered in Scotland has limited partners at least one of those must have an active UK bank account.
(3) In this section_
a __imited partnership registered in Scotland_ means a partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907;
__eneral partner_ has the meaning given in section 4(2) of the Limited Partnership Act 1907;
__imited partner_ has the meaning given in section 4(2A) of the Limited Partnership Act 1907.__(Alison Thewliss.)

