S6M-16092.2: As an amendment to motion S6M-16092 in the name of Angus Robertson (Valuing Culture: Scotland's Support to the Culture Sector), leave out from second &ldquo;welcomes&rdquo; to end and insert &ldquo;acknowledges the scale of the crisis that the culture sector has been suffering over a number of years; notes that the Scottish Government has not held a debate on support for the culture sector in the current parliamentary session until now; welcomes the intention to increase the culture budget by &pound;34 million in 2025-26, following the record budget settlement of &pound;47.7 billion to the Scottish Government from the UK Labour administration; notes the observation by the Constitution, Europe, External Affairs and Culture Committee that the culture sector&rsquo;s &lsquo;confidence remains low due to the lack of clarity from the Scottish Government regarding its priorities for the additional investment&rsquo;, and believes that Scotland&rsquo;s cultural communities must be supported to continue to develop and innovate in exhibition, performance and participation in Scotland&rsquo;s artistic life.&rdquo;

