S6M-16488.2: As an amendment to motion S6M-16488 in the name of Tom Arthur (Employer National Insurance Contributions), leave out from "recognises" to end and insert &ldquo;welcomes the record &pound;5.2 billion of additional funding for Scotland delivered as a result of the UK Government&rsquo;s Autumn Budget; agrees with the STUC that the additional positive measures that are set out in the draft Scottish Budget 2025-26 are &lsquo;dependent on UK Government funding&rsquo;; regrets that the fiscal changes called for by the Scottish Government would significantly reduce the level of funding available to Scotland&rsquo;s public services; understands that the First Minister has publicly advocated for a cut to Scotland&rsquo;s budget of &pound;636 million; regrets that the Scottish National Party administration&rsquo;s failure to grow Scotland&rsquo;s economy has negatively impacted the level of funding available in the Scottish Budget over many years; understands that decisions around the level of staffing in Scotland&rsquo;s public services are devolved to the Scottish Government, and calls on the Scottish Government to ensure that the record funding delivered by the UK Government reaches the frontline services that&nbsp;need&nbsp;it&nbsp;most.&rdquo;

