S6M-19756.1: As an amendment to motion S6M-19756 in the name of Daniel Johnson (Scotland's Skills System), leave out from &ldquo;, with better&rdquo; to end and insert &ldquo;; believes that this must be underpinned by a demand-led skills system that equips young people with the qualifications that employers need to grow Scotland&rsquo;s economy; notes that the Scottish National Party administration has failed to pass on over &pound;170 million of Apprenticeship Levy funding and has provided around 10,000 fewer apprenticeship places than learning providers requested, contributing to a widening skills gap in key sectors including hospitality, construction, engineering and care; further notes that colleges have faced a 20% real-terms funding cut, leading to job losses, falling student numbers and financial instability, and calls for urgent reform to invest in colleges, fix Scotland&rsquo;s broken apprenticeship system, address skills shortages and allow local employers to shape training that matches their workforce needs.&rdquo;

